title: GET /repos/:repo/slow
tags: [[HTTP endpoint]] [[Slow log]]
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: Reads the repository's slow log, both sources merged, newest first; DELETE empties it.

```
GET    /repos/:repo/slow?limit=<n>&since_ms=<ms>
DELETE /repos/:repo/slow
```

`GET` reads both sources merged, ''newest first'', at most `limit` entries
(default 50, capped at 500), keeping only those at or after `since_ms` when
given. The daemon reads the GUI's file too; it never writes it. Answers
`{"entries": [...], "truncated": <bool>}`, `truncated` saying the limit cut the
result short.

`DELETE` empties the log — both sources and their `.old` files — and answers
`{"cleared": <n>}`. Starting from an empty log is the normal way to reproduce a
slowdown on purpose.
